      "role": "user",
      "content": "Can BONOBO run with sparsify on at a 0.01 confidence level and delta fixed at 0.5 for my 18 log-transformed, centered endometriosis samples?"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"log-transformed\" -- not available here as asked. BONOBO's log_transformed needs an explicit true or false value; \"log-transformed\" is unresolved. BONOBO itself can still run, with its own settings instead -- an alternative, not the setting you asked for.\n\n**BONOBO**. BONOBO applies Bayesian estimation and shrinkage to sample-specific gene-gene co-expression. It does not model uncertain TF-binding/motif priors or return TF-to-gene regulatory edges. A shared probabilistic philosophy does not make these scientific outputs interchangeable.\n\nYou would need expression matrix. The analysis would provide inferred gene-to-gene associations; p-value matrix paired with a sample-specific gene-gene co-expression result.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
